Dear Alderperson <%= @name %>,

The City has extended street sweeping through Dec. 17—about a month past its usual Thanksgiving cutoff—to catch lingering leaves (Sun-Times, Nov. 19: https://chicago.suntimes.com/news/2026/11/19/chicago-extends-street-sweeping-to-week-before-christmas-as-leaves-linger-on-city-trees). Extra sweeps will be scheduled ad hoc based on weather and crew capacity.

When we reached out to the City's Open Data team, they informed us that the Department of Streets and Sanitation will NOT be updating the 2026 schedule dataset (https://data.cityofchicago.org/Sanitation/Street-Sweeping-Schedule-2026/u5ai-3efk/about_data) that <%= ENV["SITE_NAME"] %> (<%= ENV["SITE_URL"] %>) relies upon. Unfortunately, this means that schedules and email alerts on our site will miss those extra sweeps.

We have emailed subscribers in Ward <%= @ward %> to watch for temporary orange signs through Dec. 17. We also included your office's contact information so residents with feedback about late-season sweeping and the lack of a reliable schedule can reach you directly.

We wanted your office to have a heads-up in case constituents reach out. Thank you for helping to keep Chicago's streets clean!

Please note that <%= ENV["SITE_NAME"] %> is not affiliated with the City of Chicago.
<%= render "shared/email_footer", signoff: "Best regards,", coffee_link: false %>
